  "policy_append": " Device601 log follow-up (30 October 2026): validate one-to-seven-byte vertex uploads on iOS; retain the eight-byte weak prefix for larger ranges and all previous compatibility settings. Sampler-mask and inflater prototypes were withdrawn after host regressions. Source-only, no new Core, IPA or iPhone FPS result. Device601 open-issue continuation (30 October 2026): serialize internal SELF boots off UIKit with bounded save-completion handoff and stale-session guards; collect decrementer interrupts during full-MFC waits and retain host wake notifications; snapshot true iOS MoltenVK color-attachment feedback aliases even for single-TEX shaders. Exact host-only SPU compatibility mapping preserves existing JIT identities. Source and host tests only; Metal loading time, BO2 multiplayer, GOW3 introduction and AC torch rendering remain unverified on device; feedback copies may cost performance. No new Core, IPA, CI or release.",
